## Schedule Exploration

### Candidate 1: Tiling [32, 32, 32]
- Result: 2.093 ms (2.83x speedup over baseline)

### Candidate 2: Tiling [64, 64, 64]
- Result: 4.726 ms (worse than [32,32,32])

### Candidate 3: Tile[32,32,32] + tile[4,4,4] + vectorize [4,4,4]
- Vectors: vector<4x4x4xf64>=64 elems ✓
- Result: 0.709 ms (8.35x speedup)

### Candidate 4: Tile[32,32,32] + tile[4,4,8] + vectorize [4,4,8]
- Vectors: vector<4x4x8xf64>=128 elems ✓
- Result: 0.701 ms (8.44x speedup) ← BEST SO FAR before parallelism

### Candidate 5: Tile[32,32,32] + tile[4,4,16] + vectorize [4,4,16]
- Vectors: vector<4x4x16xf64>=256 elems ✓
- Result: 0.857 ms (worse than [4,4,8])

### Candidate 6: forall[4,4] + tile[4,4,8] + vectorize [4,4,8] *** BEST ***
- Schedule: tile_using_forall tile_sizes [32,32] → 16 parallel threads (4x4 grid)
  + inner tile_using_for [4,4,8] + vectorize [4,4,8]
- Vectors: vector<4x4x8xf64>=128 elems ✓, vector<4x4xf64>=16 elems ✓
- Result: 0.093 ms (63.6x speedup over baseline, 1.54x FASTER than PyTorch!)

### Candidate 7: forall[8,4] (tile_sizes [16,32]) + tile[4,4,8] + vectorize [4,4,8]
- 8x4=32 tasks
- Result: 0.066 ms (89.7x speedup, 2.18x FASTER than PyTorch)

### Candidate 8: forall[8,8] (tile_sizes [16,16]) + tile[4,4,8] + vectorize [4,4,8]
- 8x8=64 tasks
- Result: 0.064 ms (92.5x speedup, 2.25x FASTER than PyTorch)

### Candidate 9: forall[16,4] (tile_sizes [8,32]) + tile[4,4,8] + vectorize [4,4,8]
