### Candidate 17: K-first tile[0,0,64] + forall[16,16] + tile[4,8,16] + vectorize [4,8,16]
- Pre-tile the K dimension with size 64 before parallelization
- Result: 0.055 ms (worse — extra K tiling adds loop overhead without benefit)

### Candidate 18: forall[32,32] (tile_sizes [4,4]) + tile[4,4,16] + vectorize [4,4,16]
- 32x32=1024 tasks, each only 4x4 block
- Result: 0.060 ms (worse — too fine-grained task decomposition)

## Unrolling Phase (Starting from Candidate 15)

### Candidate 19: forall[16,16] + tile[4,8,16] + vectorize [4,8,16] + loop.unroll K factor=4 *** FINAL BEST ***
- Added 4x unrolling on the inner K reduction loop (%loops2#2)
- Exposes ILP across 4 FMA operations per SIMD iteration
- Result: 0.039 ms (151.8x speedup over baseline, 3.70x FASTER than PyTorch!)

### Candidate 20: forall[16,16] + tile[4,8,16] + vectorize [4,8,16] + loop.unroll K factor=16 (full unroll)
- Full unroll eliminates the K loop entirely (16 iterations)
- Result: 0.050 ms (worse — code size explosion reduces instruction cache efficiency)

---

## FINAL RESULT

### Best Schedule: Candidate 19
- **Transformation sequence**: tile_using_forall [8,8] + tile_using_for [4,8,16] + vectorize [4,8,16] + loop.unroll K×4
- **Parallel grid**: 16×16 = 256 tasks (each handles an 8×8 block of C)
- **Inner register tile**: 4 M rows × 8 N cols × 16 K slice
- **Vectors**: vector<4x8x16xf64>=512 elems (rank-3, at limit ✓), vector<4x8xf64>=32 elems ✓
- **K unroll factor**: 4 (optimal; full 16x unroll was worse)

### Measured Times
- MLIR baseline:   5.917 ms
- PyTorch ref:     0.143 ms
- Best result:     0.039 ms

### Speedup
- vs MLIR baseline: 151.8x
- vs PyTorch:        3.70x (FASTER than PyTorch!)

